    "CI_5_predictive_versus_causal_state": {
      "registered_subfamily": "A->C,B->A,B->C",
      "why": "B confounds A and C, so the observational conditional and the interventional response are different objects",
      "models_examined": 78125,
      "excluded_non_positive": 75938,
      "relation_counts": {
        "EQUAL": 243,
        "PREDICTIVE_STRICTLY_REFINES": 486,
        "CAUSAL_STRICTLY_REFINES": 0,
        "INCOMPARABLE": 1458
      },
      "proof_of_the_zero": "CAUSAL_STRICTLY_REFINES is 0 by a structural argument, not by a failed search. The causal/control state depends on the context `b` alone, so its partition has at most 2 blocks and separates exactly the two values of `b`. For it to STRICTLY refine the predictive partition, the predictive partition would have to be strictly coarser, i.e. the single block -- all four conditionals p(C=1|a,b) equal. But then the two causal vectors are equal as well and the causal partition is also the single block, so the relation is EQUAL and not strict. The count is therefore provably 0 at this scope rather than merely unobserved.",
      "witnesses": {
        "EQUAL": {
          "theta_over_4": [
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1
          ],
          "predictive_partition": [
            "A0B0|A0B1|A1B0|A1B1"
          ],
          "causal_partition": [
            "A0B0|A0B1|A1B0|A1B1"
          ]
        },
        "INCOMPARABLE": {
          "theta_over_4": [
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            2
          ],
          "predictive_partition": [
            "A0B0|A0B1|A1B0",
            "A1B1"
          ],
          "causal_partition": [
            "A0B0|A1B0",
            "A0B1|A1B1"
          ]
        },
        "PREDICTIVE_STRICTLY_REFINES": {
          "theta_over_4": [
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            1,
            2,
            2
          ],
          "predictive_partition": [
            "A0B0|A0B1",
            "A1B0|A1B1"
          ],
          "causal_partition": [
            "A0B0|A0B1|A1B0|A1B1"
          ]
        }
      },
      "note": "the causal/control state groups contexts by the whole interventional response vector, because a decision maker must compare the arms; the predictive state groups them by the single conditional at the factual arm"
    },
